---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import ThemeHead from '../../components/ThemeHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { guideSections } from '../../data/guide.js';
import '../../styles/main.css';
import '../../styles/themes.css';
import '../../styles/guide.css';
---

<Page title="Colour guide — Solai" description="Explore proposed semantic colour assignments for interfaces, code, prose, editors and terminals across every Solai flavour and mode." flavor="blue">
  <ThemeHead slot="head" />
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main" class="guide-page">
    <header class="wrap guide-intro">
      <h1>Colour in context.</h1>
      <p class="guide-lede">The same hue can mark a destination, a type, a change or a line of prose. Explore its meaning in each context, with the example beside its colour roles.</p>
      <p>These colour assignments are guide-only proposals. They do not change the exported palette.</p>
      <div class="guide-meta">
        <p id="guide-selection" aria-live="polite">Five flavours · Dark &amp; Light</p>
        <a href="/palette/" data-theme-link>Explore the source palette ↗</a>
      </div>
      <p id="guide-status" role="status" hidden>Loading palette data…</p>
      <noscript><p class="guide-noscript">JavaScript is needed to resolve the live-colour examples and role values. No specimens have loaded. You can still read the guide’s descriptions, <a href="/palette/">visit the palette page</a> or <a href="/downloads/flavor-studies.json">download the complete palette data</a>.</p></noscript>
      <p class="guide-reference">Structure inspired by <a href="https://madoromi.moonwit.ch/#palettes/guide">Madoromi’s palette guide ↗</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="wrap guide-nav" aria-label="Guide sections">
      {guideSections.map(section => <a href={`#${section.id}`}>{section.title}</a>)}
    </nav>

    <div class="wrap guide-sections">
      {guideSections.map((section, index) => (
        <section id={section.id} class="guide-section" data-guide-section={section.id} aria-labelledby={`${section.id}-heading`}>
          <header class="guide-section-header">
            <div>
              <span class="guide-section-number" aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <h2 id={`${section.id}-heading`}>{section.title}</h2>
            </div>
          </header>
          <p class="guide-section-description">{section.description}</p>
          <div class="guide-ready" hidden>
            <div class="guide-study-body">
              <figure class="guide-example">
                <figcaption>{section.title} example</figcaption>
                <div class="guide-specimen" data-guide-specimen></div>
              </figure>
              <div class="guide-role-group">
                <h3>Colour roles</h3>
                <div class="guide-role-list" data-guide-roles></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
    <aside class="wrap guide-notes" aria-label="Reading the guide">
      <h2>Read the role, not just the hue.</h2>
      <p>A red syntax token is not automatically an error. Status examples keep green for success and additions, yellow for warnings, red for danger and removals, and blue for information. Labels and symbols carry the meaning alongside colour.</p>
      <p>ANSI slots are suggested mappings: applications decide how to use them. Dark or softened slots are shown as colour tiles with contrasting labels, not as a promise that every slot works as small foreground text. Recheck contrast on your own surfaces.</p>
      <p>The header changes flavour and mode across all eight contexts. Use the section links to bookmark or share a context.</p>
      <p>Need the unchanged values? <a href="/downloads/flavor-studies.json">Download the complete palette data</a> or <a href="/downloads/flavors.css">the canonical theme CSS</a>.</p>
    </aside>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
  <script>
    import '../../scripts/guide.js';
  </script>
</Page>
